# Furkin website rules

Sources: docs/README.md, docs/WEBSITE.md (behaviour), docs/design/ (visuals). Designs win on visuals; WEBSITE.md wins on behaviour and data.

## Build
- For every page, find its row in docs/design/SCREENS.md, match the PNG and open the HTML for exact spacing. Check 1440 and 390 wide, light and dark.
- Styling comes from styles/tokens.css, styles/components.css and styles/site.css (copied from docs/design/styles). Use their classes; add new rules to site.css in the same style. No Tailwind, no CSS-in-JS, no new colour values.
- Colours: role tokens only (background, surface, ink, muted, primary, done, accent, action, on-action, on-fill, danger, shadow). Never a hex in a component.
- Only the colour profiles toy changes data-profile, and only on its own container.
- Server components by default. The toy, the theme toggle and the waitlist form are the only client components.
- Icons from components/Icon.tsx (docs/design/icons). No emoji anywhere.

## Data and security
- Supabase is shared with the app. Never create migrations or run SQL against it from here; the schema lives in the app repository (docs/db/website.sql is the hand-over).
- The service role key is server-only. Waitlist responses never reveal whether an email already exists. Invite pages show names only for valid invites.

## Copy
- All strings in content/en.ts (start from docs/design/content/en.ts). Plain labels, playful headlines, no em dashes, metric units, 24-hour time.

## Quality
- Works from 360 px with no horizontal scroll. One breakpoint at 860 px.
- prefers-reduced-motion turns off all motion. Visible focus rings. Every icon-only button has an aria-label.
- Lighthouse 95+ on every page; landing page JavaScript under 150 KB gzipped.

## Questions
- If the docs don't settle something, leave TODO(question) and list it in your summary. Don't guess.
